  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 213 AM MDT WED SEP 9 2026\nLatest models move a deep, compact upper low off the WA coast \nrapidly inland across OR Saturday, then right through our CWA \nSaturday night, and into MT Sunday. What makes this unusual is \nhow fast the low moves for a closed system, and for that reason\nwe are expecting a strong cold front to pass through our CWA \nSaturday evening, with showers, chance of thunderstorms, strong \nwinds, and rapidly falling temperatures. No highlights will \nissued just yet as the event is still 4 days away, but \nconfidence is growing with models already in good agreement. \nShowers, possibly heavy, will continue Sunday morning as \nmoisture wraps around the northern and western flanks of the \neastward-moving upper low. By late Sunday our western zones \nshould clear, and Sunday night looks clear and cold CWA-wide, \nexcept for valley fog early Monday morning. Then sunny and \nwarmer Monday before the next upper trough digs SSW-ward from\nBC and forms another low off the WA/OR coast.  Tuesday and \nWednesday should be dry and warming as models (especially GFS) \nkeep that low off the coast.",
